<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114115" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χλᾰμύς</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ύδος</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἡ</span>: acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χλαμύδα,</span> also <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χλάμυν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sapph.
					674
				</span></i>
			:—<i>short mantle,</i> worn prop. by horsemen,
				<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				7.4.4
			</span></i>; borrowed with the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέτασος</span>
			from Thessaly, <i><span class="en">
				Philem.
				34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				10.124
			</span></i>; but said to be Macedonian, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				500
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phylarch.
				62J.
			</span></i>; worn by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔφηβοι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philem.
			</span></i> l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.282
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Theod.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάτηρ σε . . δῶρον ἐς Ἅιδαν
				ὀκτωκαιδεκέταν ἐστόλισεν χλαμύδι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				7.468
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χλαμύδεσσ᾽ ἀμφεμμένοι,</span>
			of ephebi, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IGRom.</u>
				4.360.35
			</span></i> (Pergam., <span class="entity">ii A. D.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ
				χλαμύδος,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ ἐφήβου</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.752f
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				754f
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ χλαμύδος . . ᾤχετ᾽ ἐς Ἅιδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(7).447.6
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Amorgos</span>); worn by Hermes, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Tim.</u>
				30
			</span></i>; also by Eros, <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
			</span></i> l.c. (v. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				10.124
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				1.6
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				12.78
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>military cloak,</i> of foot-soldiers, <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				331
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Phil.</u>
				11
			</span></i>, etc.; of heralds, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				987
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of <i>the
				general's cloak,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Vit.</u>
				p.27J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Per.</u>
				35
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lys.</u>
				13
			</span></i>, etc.; worn by kings, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Demetr.</u>
				42
			</span></i>, etc.; by tragic kings and heroes, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>JTr.</u>
				41
			</span></i>; by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σειληνοί</span> in a
			procession, <i><span class="en">
				Callix.
				2
			</span></i>: = Lat. <i>paludamentum,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				59.17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				60.17
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				4.7.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cod.Theod.</u>
				14.10.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> a civilian's
				<i>mantle,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PCair.Zen.
				263.2
			</span></i>, al. <span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				2.402
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				 ii 16
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				X.Eph.
				1.8
			</span></i> cod., <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1288.24
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A. D.)</span>. (For its shape cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				26
			</span></i>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
